<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Release-scoped upgrade data for Darpan 1.4.0.
Generated from backend compare range: v1.3.0..HEAD, then reviewed.
Records must also live in generic source data files under runtime/component/darpan/data/.
Load with: ./gradlew loadDarpanUpgradeData

PREREQUISITE: this file is release-scoped and carries ONLY the records new in 1.4.0. It does not
re-carry the 1.3.0 record (the OMS connector's filterParameterName). An environment that never
loaded data/releases/1.3.0/upgrade-data.xml must load that file first, or source exclusion filters
stay inert there even after 1.4.0 is deployed.

ORDERING NOTE: the generator sorts records by source file, which this release happens to agree with
— DarpanSystemSourceSeedData.xml sorts before SourceSystemConnectorSeedData.xml, so the
OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS Enumeration lands before the SourceSystemConnector row whose systemEnumId
references it. That alignment is coincidence, not a guarantee. Re-check parent-before-child by hand
after every regeneration.

SCOPE DRIFT: the header range above describes the 1.4.0 cut, but records added after that cut
accumulate here until the next release regenerates the file (the ArtifactGroupMember row, the
OMS_RECON_ORDERS pair, the OMS_RETURNS pair, and the SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS pair below all post-date
it). Re-derive the range at the next cut rather than trusting this header.

OPERATOR IMPACT: additive records only — nothing existing is modified, so loading this file changes
no current reconciliation behaviour.

- Two Enumerations and one SourceSystemConnector row register HotWax transfer orders as a selectable
  source system. Until they load, transfer orders do not appear as a source-system option and any
  saved configuration naming them cannot resolve a connector.
- One Enumeration and one SourceSystemConnector row register the OMS reconciliationOrders endpoint
  (DAR-BE-018) as a SECOND, opt-in OMS orders source. The existing OMS row is untouched and stays
  the default, so no rule set moves onto the new endpoint by loading this file; adoption is an
  explicit per-rule-set change to sourceConfigType HOTWAX_OMS_REST_RECON. Until these load, that
  connector cannot be selected and its extract service is not dispatchable (the security allow-list
  is derived from enabled connector rows).
- One Enumeration and one SourceSystemConnector row register the OMS reconciliationReturns endpoint
  (DAR-BE-018) as a NEW source system, OMS_RETURNS. This is additive capability, not a migration —
  Darpan did not reconcile returns before this row, so no existing rule set changes behaviour. Until
  these load, OMS_RETURNS does not appear as a selectable source and its extract service is not
  dispatchable (the security allow-list is derived from enabled connector rows). filterParameterName
  is present so the returnChannelEnumId exclusion (§5) can dispatch once a tenant configures it.
- One Enumeration and one SourceSystemConnector row register the Shopify per-order refund/return id
  extractor (DAR-BE-018 task 9) as a NEW source system, SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS, exposing
  extract#ShopifyOrderReturnRefs. Additive capability sharing the SHOPIFY_REMOTE remote and the
  canonical ShopifyAuthConfig entity with the existing SHOPIFY row; no existing rule set changes
  behaviour. Until these load, SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS does not appear as a selectable source and its
  extract service is not dispatchable (the security allow-list is derived from enabled connector
  rows). No filterParameterName: this connector carries no tenant exclusion rules.

The AUT_WIN_STATE row backs a window mode that is deliberately NOT offered in the UI in this
release — list#AutomationSourceOptions filters it out, because the per-source status list it needs
has no write path yet. The row is loaded now so the enum is in place when that surface ships;
loading it exposes nothing to operators.
-->
<entity-facade-xml type="darpan-seed">
    <!-- Added records from data/AutomationSeedData.xml -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="AUT_WIN_STATE" enumTypeId="AutomationRelWindow" enumCode="STATE_BASED" description="State based (no date window)" sequenceNum="8"/>
    <!-- CORRECTIONS to two rows that already exist in every deployed environment. Both are
         create-or-update by PK, so these restate the row with the corrected description and change
         nothing else.

         SHOPIFY's stored description is the shouty "SHOPIFY", which is what a deployed environment
         renders wherever a system is named — the run-result page's "Extracting SHOPIFY",
         "Missing from SHOPIFY", and the compared-files labels. OMS never showed the same problem
         only because SettingsFacadeSupport.normalizeSystemSourceOption HARDCODES description
         "HotWax" for OMS/HOTWAX options, overriding whatever the database holds; Shopify has no
         such override and falls through to the raw row. Restating OMS here too keeps the seed file
         and the database in agreement rather than relying on that override.

         NOTE these fix FUTURE runs only. ReconciliationOutputSupport reads file labels from
         metadata.get("file1Label"), i.e. the label is stamped into each run's output document when
         the run executes. Historical runs keep the name they were stamped with, by decision
         (2026-08-13) — backfilling would mean rewriting stored output documents. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="OMS" enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource" enumCode="HOTWAX" description="HotWax" sequenceNum="1"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SHOPIFY" enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource" enumCode="SHOPIFY" description="Shopify" sequenceNum="2"/>
    <!-- Added records from data/DarpanSystemSourceSeedData.xml.
         Precedes the SourceSystemConnector row below: that row's systemEnumId references this enum.
         parentEnumId="OMS" groups this endpoint under OMS for the two-step source picker (system,
         then endpoint) — see list#AutomationSourceOptions / darpan-ui's darpanSystems.ts.
         Both parents above load first, satisfying the parentEnumId self-reference. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS" enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource" enumCode="HOTWAX_TRANSFER_ORDERS" description="HotWax Transfer Orders" sequenceNum="6" parentEnumId="OMS"/>
    <!-- DAR-BE-018. Same parent-before-child constraint as the row above: the OMS_RECON_ORDERS
         SourceSystemConnector further down references this enum by systemEnumId. Same
         parentEnumId="OMS" picker grouping as above. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource" enumCode="HOTWAX_RECON_ORDERS" description="HotWax Orders (Reconciliation API)" sequenceNum="7" parentEnumId="OMS"/>
    <!-- DAR-BE-018. Same parent-before-child constraint: the OMS_RETURNS SourceSystemConnector
         further down references this enum by systemEnumId. Same parentEnumId="OMS" picker
         grouping as above. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="OMS_RETURNS" enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource" enumCode="HOTWAX_RETURNS" description="HotWax Returns (Reconciliation API)" sequenceNum="8" parentEnumId="OMS"/>
    <!-- DAR-BE-018 task 9. Same parent-before-child constraint: the SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS
         SourceSystemConnector further down references this enum by systemEnumId.
         parentEnumId="SHOPIFY" groups it under SHOPIFY for the two-step source picker. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource" enumCode="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" description="Shopify Order Return References" sequenceNum="9" parentEnumId="SHOPIFY"/>
    <!-- Added records from data/SecuritySeedData.xml.
         Parent ArtifactGroup DARPAN_AUTH_API already exists in every deployed environment (it has carried
         login#Session since before 1.3.0), so this row has no forward FK reference and needs no reordering.
         Registers the anonymous forced-password-change entry point alongside the other pre-session auth
         services. Until it loads, a fresh install and an upgraded install disagree on the contents of the
         anonymous auth fence. -->
    <moqui.security.ArtifactGroupMember artifactGroupId="DARPAN_AUTH_API" artifactName="facade.AuthFacadeServices.change#ExpiredPassword" artifactTypeEnumId="AT_SERVICE" inheritAuthz="Y"/>
    <!-- Added records from data/SourceSystemConnectorSeedData.xml -->
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS" extractServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsTransferOrders" dateFromParameterName="windowStart" dateToParameterName="windowEnd" expectedSourceConfigType="HOTWAX_OMS_REST_TRANSFER" configParameterName="omsRestSourceConfigId" configEntityName="darpan.hotwax.HotWaxOmsRestSourceConfig" remoteId="HOTWAX_ORDERS_API" endpointLabel="Orders API (Transfer Orders)" sendUrlTemplate="{baseUrl}/rest/s1/oms/orders" remoteSendServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsTransferOrders" systemAliases="OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS,HOTWAX_TRANSFER_ORDERS,DAR_SYS_OMS_TO" preserveWindowInstants="N" keepFieldsParameterName="keepRecordFields" keepFieldsBase="orderId,orderName,orderDate,statusId,originFacilityId,grandTotal,currencyUom" filterParameterName="sourceFilters" windowFieldName="orderDate" supportsStateExtract="Y" statusParameterName="orderStatusIds" healthCheckServiceName="facade.HotWaxOmsFacadeServices.probe#HotWaxOmsConnection" enabled="Y"/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" extractServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReconciliationOrders" dateFromParameterName="windowStart" dateToParameterName="windowEnd" expectedSourceConfigType="HOTWAX_OMS_REST_RECON" configParameterName="omsRestSourceConfigId" configEntityName="darpan.hotwax.HotWaxOmsRestSourceConfig" remoteId="HOTWAX_ORDERS_API" endpointLabel="Reconciliation Orders API" sendUrlTemplate="{baseUrl}/rest/s1/oms/reconciliationOrders" remoteSendServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReconciliationOrders" systemAliases="OMS_RECON_ORDERS,HOTWAX_RECON_ORDERS,DAR_SYS_OMS_RECON" preserveWindowInstants="N" keepFieldsParameterName="keepRecordFields" keepFieldsBase="orderId,orderName,externalId,grandTotal,orderDate,statusId" filterParameterName="sourceFilters" healthCheckServiceName="facade.HotWaxOmsFacadeServices.probe#HotWaxOmsConnection" enabled="Y"/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" extractServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReturns" dateFromParameterName="windowStart" dateToParameterName="windowEnd" expectedSourceConfigType="HOTWAX_OMS_REST_RETURNS" configParameterName="omsRestSourceConfigId" configEntityName="darpan.hotwax.HotWaxOmsRestSourceConfig" remoteId="HOTWAX_ORDERS_API" endpointLabel="Reconciliation Returns API" sendUrlTemplate="{baseUrl}/rest/s1/oms/reconciliationReturns" remoteSendServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReturns" systemAliases="OMS_RETURNS,HOTWAX_RETURNS,DAR_SYS_OMS_RETURNS" preserveWindowInstants="N" keepFieldsParameterName="keepRecordFields" keepFieldsBase="returnId,externalId,orderExternalId,statusId,entryDate,returnTotal,currencyUomId,returnChannelEnumId" filterParameterName="sourceFilters" healthCheckServiceName="facade.HotWaxOmsFacadeServices.probe#HotWaxOmsConnection" enabled="Y"/>
    <!-- DAR-BE-018 task 9: Shopify per-order refund/return id sets, cursor-paginated (see
         SourceSystemConnectorSeedData.xml for the full row rationale). -->
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" extractServiceName="reconciliation.ShopifyOrderExtractionServices.extract#ShopifyOrderReturnRefs" dateFromParameterName="windowStart" dateToParameterName="windowEnd" expectedSourceConfigType="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS_API" configParameterName="shopifyAuthConfigId" configEntityName="darpan.shopify.ShopifyAuthConfig" remoteId="SHOPIFY_REMOTE" endpointLabel="Shopify Return References" systemAliases="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS,SHOPIFY_RETURNS,DAR_SYS_SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" preserveWindowInstants="N" enabled="Y"/>
</entity-facade-xml>
